issue.body:
Component(s): Core

## Description

A Spark read failed with `StackOverflowError` in `org.apache.parquet.hadoop.ParquetFileReader.readNextRowGroup()` while reading a Parquet file containing many consecutive empty row groups. The failure investigation recorded 3,263 row groups, 3,199 of them empty, with a longest consecutive run of 2,500 empty groups. The stack trace repeatedly contained `ParquetFileReader.readNextRowGroup`.

The expected behavior is to skip empty row groups and return the next non-empty group, or `null` at EOF, without growing the call stack with the number of skipped groups.

## Cause and affected paths

In [readNextRowGroup](https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/blob/a449253a458a25a0ad122b250e9964072798527e/parquet-hadoop/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/hadoop/ParquetFileReader.java#L1137), an empty group raises `ParquetEmptyBlockException`. The catch block advances to the next group and recursively calls the same method:

```java
} catch (ParquetEmptyBlockException e) {
  LOG.warn("Read empty block at index {} from {}", currentBlock, getFile());
  advanceToNextBlock();
  return readNextRowGroup();
}
```

Each consecutive empty group adds another stack frame. Java does not eliminate these recursive calls, so a sufficiently long run can exhaust the thread stack. The failure threshold depends on the JVM and thread stack size.

[readNextFilteredRowGroup](https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/blob/a449253a458a25a0ad122b250e9964072798527e/parquet-hadoop/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/hadoop/ParquetFileReader.java#L1526) also calls itself recursively when a group is empty or its column-index-filtered row ranges contain no matching rows. The latter path also grows the call stack with each skipped group, even when the groups are non-empty.

The recursive empty-group handling is present in the inspected 1.13.1, 1.15.2, 1.16.0, 1.17.1, and 1.18.1 tags and the master revision linked above.

## Suggested fix

Replace recursive skipping with iteration in both sequential read methods, preserving group advancement, dictionary-reader updates, and buffer ownership. Regression cases should cover many consecutive empty groups before a non-empty group, all-empty groups, trailing empty groups, and many consecutive groups with no matching column-index-filtered rows.

This follows [#2728](https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/issues/2728) (originally PARQUET-2219) and [#1018](https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/pull/1018), which added empty-group skipping. The discussion in #2728 notes that the specification does not prohibit zero-length row groups. The existing `TestParquetReaderEmptyBlock` covers up to two consecutive empty groups.

I used an AI agent to help analyze the source and draft this issue. I reviewed the final text.
